{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-83898","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116487","text":"Runefort Protocol — v0.1"}]},{"id":"blk-83899","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116488","marks":["bold"],"text":"A layout protocol for living, file-backed, tile-grid web apps."}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83901","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116489","marks":["bold"],"text":"Part of the [&] Protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-116490","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-116491","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/ECOSYSTEM.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem overview"},{"id":"spn-116492","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-116493","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/THREE_PROTOCOL_STACK.md"}],"text":"Three-protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-116494","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-116495","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/STACK_COMPLETION.md"}],"text":"Stack status"}]}],"id":"blk-83900","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-83902","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116496","text":"Status: draft v0.1 Owner: runefort.com Date: 2026-04-25 Position: protocol-level. Independent of [&], PULSE, PRISM. May be used by them; does not require them."}]},{"id":"blk-83903","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116497","marks":["bold"],"text":"Related documents:"}]},{"id":"blk-83904","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83906","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116498","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/docs/spec/runefort.core.md"}],"text":"@runefort/core — Reference Web Component Framework v0.1"}]}],"id":"blk-83905","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83908","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116499","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/docs/spec/runefort.dsl.md"}],"text":".rune DSL — v0.1"}]}],"id":"blk-83907","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83910","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116500","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-BUILD-ORDER.md"}],"text":"Interactive Layer — Build Order"}]}],"id":"blk-83909","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83912","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116501","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-1_BYOK.md"}],"text":"RFort-1 — BYOK Modal + OpenRouter Key Storage"}]}],"id":"blk-83911","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83914","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116502","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-2_MCP.md"}],"text":"RFort-2 — MCP Proxy + Client + Connection Panel"}]}],"id":"blk-83913","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83916","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116503","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-3_CHAT.md"}],"text":"RFort-3 — Chat Panel with Fort-Aware Navigation"}]}],"id":"blk-83915","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83918","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116504","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-4_TOKENFLOWS.md"}],"text":"RFort-4 — Token Flow Animations on Edges"}]}],"id":"blk-83917","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83920","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116505","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-5_REPO_IMPORT.md"}],"text":"RFort-5 — Repo Import → Fort Generator"}]}],"id":"blk-83919","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83922","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116506","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-6_WORKSPACES.md"}],"text":"RFort-6 — Workspace Switcher + Supabase Persistence"}]}],"id":"blk-83921","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-83923","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116507","text":"0. What this is, in one paragraph"}]},{"id":"blk-83924","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116508","text":"Runefort is a small declarative protocol for describing a "},{"id":"spn-116509","marks":["bold"],"text":"tiled, file-backed UI layout"},{"id":"spn-116510","text":". You declare "},{"id":"spn-116511","marks":["italic"],"text":"rooms"},{"id":"spn-116512","text":" (tiles), "},{"id":"spn-116513","marks":["italic"],"text":"claims"},{"id":"spn-116514","text":" (file-system regions each room owns), "},{"id":"spn-116515","marks":["italic"],"text":"neighbors"},{"id":"spn-116516","text":" (adjacency for navigation), and "},{"id":"spn-116517","marks":["italic"],"text":"state bindings"},{"id":"spn-116518","text":" (how live state colors a tile). A conformant renderer compiles the declaration to a CSS grid, surfaces each claim's content for inline viewing or editing, and overlays live state. The protocol is the contract between the declaration and the renderer. Nothing more."}]},{"id":"blk-83925","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116519","text":"It is not a workforce platform. It is not a supervisor framework. It is not a graph visualization library. It is the "},{"id":"spn-116520","marks":["bold"],"text":"layout language"},{"id":"spn-116521","text":" that those things can be built with."}]},{"id":"blk-83926","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116522","text":"1. Why a protocol (not a library)"}]},{"id":"blk-83927","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83929","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116523","marks":["bold"],"text":"Renderer-portable."},{"id":"spn-116524","text":" The same "},{"id":"spn-116525","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-116526","text":" should render in Elixir/Phoenix, TypeScript/React, or static HTML. The protocol is the only thing they share."}]}],"id":"blk-83928","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83931","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116527","marks":["bold"],"text":"Diffable."},{"id":"spn-116528","text":" Layouts live in version control as text. Reviews become readable. SVG graph layouts cannot do this."}]}],"id":"blk-83930","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83933","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116529","marks":["bold"],"text":"Extensible by composition."},{"id":"spn-116530","text":" Apps add "},{"id":"spn-116531","marks":["italic"],"text":"vocabularies"},{"id":"spn-116532","text":" (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-116533","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor"},{"id":"spn-116534","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116535","marks":["code"],"text":"dashboard"},{"id":"spn-116536","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116537","marks":["code"],"text":"wiki-page"},{"id":"spn-116538","text":") on top of the core primitives. The protocol does not know about supervisors."}]}],"id":"blk-83932","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83935","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116539","marks":["bold"],"text":"No runtime layout engine required."},{"id":"spn-116540","text":" All layout is compile-time deterministic. No d3, no dagre, no jitter."}]}],"id":"blk-83934","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-83936","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116541","text":"2. Core primitives"}]},{"id":"blk-83937","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116542","text":"Four primitives. That is the entire vocabulary."}]},{"id":"blk-83938","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116543","text":"2.1 Room"}]},{"id":"blk-83939","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116544","text":"A room is a tile in the grid. It has an id, a position, a size, and arbitrary metadata."}]},{"id":"blk-83940","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"id\": \"memory\",\n  \"position\": [0, 0],\n  \"size\": [3, 2],\n  \"label\": \"memory.ex\",\n  \"meta\": {}\n}"},{"id":"blk-83941","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116545","marks":["code"],"text":"position"},{"id":"spn-116546","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-116547","marks":["code"],"text":"size"},{"id":"spn-116548","text":" are integer cell coordinates in a CSS grid. "},{"id":"spn-116549","marks":["code"],"text":"[0,0]"},{"id":"spn-116550","text":" is top-left. "},{"id":"spn-116551","marks":["code"],"text":"size: [3,2]"},{"id":"spn-116552","text":" means 3 columns wide, 2 rows tall. The renderer is free to choose the cell pixel size; the protocol only specifies cell counts."}]},{"id":"blk-83942","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116553","text":"2.2 Claim"}]},{"id":"blk-83943","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116554","text":"A claim is a file-system region a room \"owns.\" A renderer uses claims to (a) list which files belong to a room and (b) surface those files inline — either as a viewer or an editor — when the user activates the room. Optional behaviors include generating external-editor handoff URLs ("},{"id":"spn-116555","marks":["code"],"text":"vscode://"},{"id":"spn-116556","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116557","marks":["code"],"text":"cursor://"},{"id":"spn-116558","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116559","marks":["code"],"text":"zed://"},{"id":"spn-116560","text":") for users who prefer their own tools."}]},{"id":"blk-83944","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"room\": \"memory\",\n  \"pattern\": \"lib/my_app/memory/**/*.ex\",\n  \"anchor\": \"lib/my_app/forge/memory.ex#L24\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-83945","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116561","marks":["code"],"text":"pattern"},{"id":"spn-116562","text":" is a glob. "},{"id":"spn-116563","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-116564","text":" is the canonical file the room represents (the one a click on the tile opens)."}]},{"id":"blk-83946","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116565","text":"2.3 Neighbor"}]},{"id":"blk-83947","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116566","text":"A neighbor declares an adjacency between two rooms. Neighbors drive keyboard navigation ("},{"id":"spn-116567","marks":["code"],"text":"h/j/k/l"},{"id":"spn-116568","text":"), focus order, and may be rendered as connecting lines."}]},{"id":"blk-83948","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"from\": \"memory\", \"to\": \"deploy\", \"kind\": \"adjacent\" }"},{"id":"blk-83949","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116569","marks":["code"],"text":"kind"},{"id":"spn-116570","text":" is one of: "},{"id":"spn-116571","marks":["code"],"text":"adjacent"},{"id":"spn-116572","text":" (touching), "},{"id":"spn-116573","marks":["code"],"text":"linked"},{"id":"spn-116574","text":" (logical link, may not be touching), "},{"id":"spn-116575","marks":["code"],"text":"nested"},{"id":"spn-116576","text":" (one contains the other)."}]},{"id":"blk-83950","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116577","text":"2.4 State binding"}]},{"id":"blk-83951","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116578","text":"A state binding tells the renderer how to color a room based on a runtime signal. The protocol defines the "},{"id":"spn-116579","marks":["italic"],"text":"binding"},{"id":"spn-116580","text":", not the signal source — signals are pushed to the renderer over whatever transport the host app provides (WebSocket, SSE, polling, static)."}]},{"id":"blk-83952","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"room\": \"memory\",\n  \"signal\": \"kappa\",\n  \"thresholds\": [\n    { \"if\": \"< 0.3\", \"class\": \"cold\" },\n    { \"if\": \"< 0.6\", \"class\": \"warm\" },\n    { \"if\": \">= 0.6\", \"class\": \"hot\" }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-83953","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116581","marks":["code"],"text":"class"},{"id":"spn-116582","text":" is a token the renderer maps to CSS. The protocol reserves five canonical classes: "},{"id":"spn-116583","marks":["code"],"text":"cold"},{"id":"spn-116584","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116585","marks":["code"],"text":"warm"},{"id":"spn-116586","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116587","marks":["code"],"text":"hot"},{"id":"spn-116588","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116589","marks":["code"],"text":"fault"},{"id":"spn-116590","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116591","marks":["code"],"text":"idle"},{"id":"spn-116592","text":". Apps may add custom classes — renderers should ignore unknown classes gracefully (treat as "},{"id":"spn-116593","marks":["code"],"text":"cold"},{"id":"spn-116594","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-83954","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116595","text":"3. Document shape"}]},{"id":"blk-83955","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116596","text":"A complete "},{"id":"spn-116597","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-116598","text":" is just an object containing arrays of the four primitives, plus header metadata."}]},{"id":"blk-83956","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"runefort\": \"0.1\",\n  \"title\": \"my_app forge floor\",\n  \"grid\": { \"columns\": 6, \"rows\": 4 },\n  \"rooms\": [ ... ],\n  \"claims\": [ ... ],\n  \"neighbors\": [ ... ],\n  \"state_bindings\": [ ... ],\n  \"vocabulary\": \"core\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-83957","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116599","marks":["code"],"text":"grid.columns"},{"id":"spn-116600","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-116601","marks":["code"],"text":"grid.rows"},{"id":"spn-116602","text":" are the total grid dimensions. "},{"id":"spn-116603","marks":["code"],"text":"vocabulary"},{"id":"spn-116604","text":" is the name of the extension vocabulary in use; "},{"id":"spn-116605","marks":["code"],"text":"\"core\""},{"id":"spn-116606","text":" means no extensions."}]},{"id":"blk-83958","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116607","text":"4. The DSL surface (host-language sugar)"}]},{"id":"blk-83959","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116608","text":"Hosts may expose a DSL that compiles to the JSON above. The DSL is "},{"id":"spn-116609","marks":["bold"],"text":"not normative"},{"id":"spn-116610","text":" — only the JSON is. A reference Elixir DSL:"}]},{"id":"blk-83960","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"defmodule MyApp.Floor do\n  use Runefort.Layout, columns: 6, rows: 4\n\n  room :memory,\n    at: {0, 0}, size: {3, 2},\n    claims: ~r{lib/my_app/memory/},\n    anchor: \"lib/my_app/forge/memory.ex:24\"\n\n  room :deploy,\n    at: {3, 0}, size: {3, 2},\n    claims: ~r{lib/my_app/deploy/}\n\n  neighbors :memory => :deploy\n\n  bind :memory, signal: :kappa,\n    cold: \"< 0.3\", warm: \"< 0.6\", hot: \">= 0.6\"\nend"},{"id":"blk-83961","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116611","text":"A reference TypeScript DSL:"}]},{"id":"blk-83962","kind":"code","language":"ts","text":"const floor = layout({ columns: 6, rows: 4 }, [\n  room(\"memory\", { at: [0,0], size: [3,2], claims: \"lib/my_app/memory/**\" }),\n  room(\"deploy\", { at: [3,0], size: [3,2], claims: \"lib/my_app/deploy/**\" }),\n  neighbor(\"memory\", \"deploy\"),\n  bind(\"memory\", \"kappa\", { cold: \"< 0.3\", warm: \"< 0.6\", hot: \">= 0.6\" }),\n]);"},{"id":"blk-83963","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116612","text":"Both compile to the same JSON. Either is conformant. Neither is privileged."}]},{"id":"blk-83964","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116613","text":"5. Renderer contract"}]},{"id":"blk-83965","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116614","text":"A conformant renderer MUST:"}]},{"id":"blk-83966","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83968","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116615","marks":["bold"],"text":"Layout."},{"id":"spn-116616","text":" Render rooms in a CSS grid (or visually equivalent) using each room's "},{"id":"spn-116617","marks":["code"],"text":"position"},{"id":"spn-116618","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-116619","marks":["code"],"text":"size"},{"id":"spn-116620","text":". The grid MUST be deterministic — given the same JSON, the rendered DOM order MUST be stable."}]}],"id":"blk-83967","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83970","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116621","marks":["bold"],"text":"Anchors."},{"id":"spn-116622","text":" Resolve each room's "},{"id":"spn-116623","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-116624","text":" to its content (the file or content region the room represents). Activating a tile MUST surface that content — by default, inline within the host page (viewer or editor). Renderers MAY additionally offer an external-editor handoff URL as a secondary action, but inline surfacing is the canonical behavior."}]}],"id":"blk-83969","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83972","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116625","marks":["bold"],"text":"State classes."},{"id":"spn-116626","text":" Apply CSS classes from "},{"id":"spn-116627","marks":["code"],"text":"state_bindings"},{"id":"spn-116628","text":" to each room's root element. Class names MUST be predictable: "},{"id":"spn-116629","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort-state-cold"},{"id":"spn-116630","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116631","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort-state-hot"},{"id":"spn-116632","text":", etc."}]}],"id":"blk-83971","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83974","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116633","marks":["bold"],"text":"Accessibility."},{"id":"spn-116634","text":" Each room MUST be focusable (keyboard) and have a stable accessible name (the room's "},{"id":"spn-116635","marks":["code"],"text":"label"},{"id":"spn-116636","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-116637","marks":["code"],"text":"id"},{"id":"spn-116638","text":")."}]}],"id":"blk-83973","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83976","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116639","marks":["bold"],"text":"Neighbor navigation."},{"id":"spn-116640","text":" Arrow keys (or "},{"id":"spn-116641","marks":["code"],"text":"h/j/k/l"},{"id":"spn-116642","text":") MUST move focus along "},{"id":"spn-116643","marks":["code"],"text":"neighbor"},{"id":"spn-116644","text":" edges. Renderers MAY also expose mouse navigation; keyboard support is required."}]}],"id":"blk-83975","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-83977","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116645","text":"A conformant renderer SHOULD:"}]},{"id":"blk-83978","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83980","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116646","text":"Provide an inline editor (not just a read-only viewer) for the focused room's "},{"id":"spn-116647","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-116648","text":" when the host environment supports text editing."}]}],"id":"blk-83979","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83982","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116649","text":"Highlight neighbor adjacencies on hover/focus."}]}],"id":"blk-83981","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83984","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116650","text":"Re-render on signal change without full reload."}]}],"id":"blk-83983","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-83985","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116651","text":"A conformant renderer MAY:"}]},{"id":"blk-83986","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83988","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116652","text":"Add domain-specific vocabularies (see §6)."}]}],"id":"blk-83987","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83990","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116653","text":"Display additional metadata from "},{"id":"spn-116654","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-116655","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-83989","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83992","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116656","text":"Animate state class transitions."}]}],"id":"blk-83991","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-83994","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116657","text":"Offer external-editor handoff URLs ("},{"id":"spn-116658","marks":["code"],"text":"vscode://"},{"id":"spn-116659","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116660","marks":["code"],"text":"cursor://"},{"id":"spn-116661","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116662","marks":["code"],"text":"zed://"},{"id":"spn-116663","text":") as a secondary action for users who prefer their own tools. Renderers that run outside the browser (e.g. static-site generators, server-rendered HTML with no JS) MAY treat handoff as their primary surfacing strategy and still claim conformance."}]}],"id":"blk-83993","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-83995","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116664","text":"6. Vocabularies (extension points)"}]},{"id":"blk-83996","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116665","text":"The protocol's core knows nothing about supervisors, dashboards, or wikis. Apps declare a "},{"id":"spn-116666","marks":["italic"],"text":"vocabulary"},{"id":"spn-116667","text":" — a named bundle of extra fields on "},{"id":"spn-116668","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-116669","text":", extra signals, and extra state classes."}]},{"id":"blk-83997","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"runefort\": \"0.1\",\n  \"vocabulary\": \"supervisor-floor.v1\",\n  \"rooms\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"memory\",\n      \"position\": [0,0], \"size\": [3,2],\n      \"meta\": {\n        \"supervisor\": {\n          \"autonomy\": \"advise\",\n          \"uptime_seconds\": 957840,\n          \"last_action\": \"consolidated 47 nodes\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-83998","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116670","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-116671","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-116672","text":" vocabulary defines what "},{"id":"spn-116673","marks":["code"],"text":"meta.supervisor"},{"id":"spn-116674","text":" contains. A renderer that doesn't know "},{"id":"spn-116675","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-116676","text":" MUST still render the layout correctly — it just won't display the supervisor-specific overlay. "},{"id":"spn-116677","marks":["bold"],"text":"Vocabulary unknown = degrade, don't fail."}]},{"id":"blk-83999","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116678","text":"Reserved vocabularies (managed by the protocol authors):"}]},{"id":"blk-84000","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84002","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116679","marks":["code"],"text":"core"},{"id":"spn-116680","text":" — the four primitives, no extensions."}]}],"id":"blk-84001","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84004","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116681","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-116682","text":" — for [&]/Runefort supervisor workforce apps."}]}],"id":"blk-84003","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84006","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116683","marks":["code"],"text":"codebase-atlas.v1"},{"id":"spn-116684","text":" — for repository visualization apps."}]}],"id":"blk-84005","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84008","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116685","marks":["code"],"text":"dashboard-grid.v1"},{"id":"spn-116686","text":" — for metric/observability tile dashboards."}]}],"id":"blk-84007","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84009","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116687","text":"Custom vocabularies are namespaced freely ("},{"id":"spn-116688","marks":["code"],"text":"com.example.my-vocab.v1"},{"id":"spn-116689","text":"). The protocol does not require registration."}]},{"id":"blk-84010","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116690","text":"7. Non-goals"}]},{"id":"blk-84011","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116691","text":"Explicit, so the protocol stays small:"}]},{"id":"blk-84012","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84014","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116692","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a graph visualization protocol."},{"id":"spn-116693","text":" Force-directed layouts, dagre, hierarchies — out of scope. Runefort is grids only. If you need a graph, use a graph tool."}]}],"id":"blk-84013","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84016","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116694","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a state-management protocol."},{"id":"spn-116695","text":" How signals are computed, where they live, how they're transported — host's problem."}]}],"id":"blk-84015","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84018","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116696","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a workforce / supervision framework."},{"id":"spn-116697","text":" That's a "},{"id":"spn-116698","marks":["italic"],"text":"vocabulary"},{"id":"spn-116699","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-116700","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-116701","text":"), built on top."}]}],"id":"blk-84017","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84020","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116702","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a presentation framework."},{"id":"spn-116703","text":" No theming spec, no animation spec. CSS is the renderer's job."}]}],"id":"blk-84019","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84022","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116704","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not coupled to [&], PULSE, or PRISM."},{"id":"spn-116705","text":" A "},{"id":"spn-116706","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-116707","text":" describing a recipe app is fully conformant."}]}],"id":"blk-84021","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84023","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116708","text":"8. Versioning"}]},{"id":"blk-84024","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116709","text":"Semver for the protocol itself. The top-level "},{"id":"spn-116710","marks":["code"],"text":"\"runefort\": \"0.1\""},{"id":"spn-116711","text":" field is the protocol version, NOT the renderer version."}]},{"id":"blk-84025","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84027","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116712","marks":["bold"],"text":"Major bump"},{"id":"spn-116713","text":" = breaking JSON shape change."}]}],"id":"blk-84026","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84029","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116714","marks":["bold"],"text":"Minor bump"},{"id":"spn-116715","text":" = additive (new optional fields, new reserved vocabularies, new state classes)."}]}],"id":"blk-84028","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84031","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116716","marks":["bold"],"text":"Patch"},{"id":"spn-116717","text":" = clarification only, no behavior change."}]}],"id":"blk-84030","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84032","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116718","text":"A renderer MUST refuse documents with a major version it does not support. A renderer SHOULD render documents with a higher minor version, ignoring fields it does not recognize."}]},{"id":"blk-84033","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116719","text":"9. Reference framework — "},{"id":"spn-116720","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"}]},{"id":"blk-84034","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116721","text":"The canonical browser-side reference implementation is "},{"id":"spn-116722","marks":["bold"],"text":"`@runefort/core`"},{"id":"spn-116723","text":": a small set of Web Components ("},{"id":"spn-116724","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-floor>"},{"id":"spn-116725","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116726","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-room>"},{"id":"spn-116727","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116728","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-claim>"},{"id":"spn-116729","text":", "},{"id":"spn-116730","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-link>"},{"id":"spn-116731","text":") implementing this protocol with no framework dependency. ~5KB minified target. Specified in "},{"id":"spn-116732","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.core.md"},{"id":"spn-116733","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-84035","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116734","text":"Why a reference framework, not just a renderer:"}]},{"id":"blk-84036","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84038","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116735","marks":["bold"],"text":"Zero-build adoption."},{"id":"spn-116736","text":" Drop one "},{"id":"spn-116737","marks":["code"],"text":"<script type=\"module\">"},{"id":"spn-116738","text":" tag into any HTML page and the protocol is rendered. No bundler, no npm, no framework."}]}],"id":"blk-84037","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84040","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116739","marks":["bold"],"text":"Universal embedding."},{"id":"spn-116740","text":" Custom Elements work inside React, Vue, Svelte, Solid, Lit, Astro, Phoenix LiveView, Rails view templates, plain HTML. The framework adapters are ~1KB each, not full reimplementations."}]}],"id":"blk-84039","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84042","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116741","marks":["bold"],"text":"Single reactivity story."},{"id":"spn-116742","text":" Property setters on "},{"id":"spn-116743","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-floor>"},{"id":"spn-116744","text":" push signal updates; rooms recompute their state class. No virtual DOM, no opinionated state library — composes with whatever the host app already uses."}]}],"id":"blk-84041","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84043","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116745","text":"Conformant alternatives may exist. "},{"id":"spn-116746","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"},{"id":"spn-116747","text":" is the reference, not the only option. A pure-Phoenix-LiveView renderer or a server-rendered static-HTML emitter are both valid conformant implementations."}]},{"id":"blk-84044","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116748","text":"9.1 Authoring surfaces"}]},{"id":"blk-84045","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116749","text":"The same protocol is reachable through three authoring surfaces, all equivalent and all round-trippable:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-84047","spans":[{"id":"spn-116750","text":"Surface"}]},{"id":"blk-84048","spans":[{"id":"spn-116751","text":"Format"}]},{"id":"blk-84049","spans":[{"id":"spn-116752","text":"Use case"}]}],"id":"blk-84046","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-84050","spans":[{"id":"spn-116753","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"}]},{"id":"blk-84051","spans":[{"id":"spn-116754","text":"JSON"}]},{"id":"blk-84052","spans":[{"id":"spn-116755","text":"Programmatic generation, tooling integration, canonical persistence"}]}],[{"id":"blk-84053","spans":[{"id":"spn-116756","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-*>"},{"id":"spn-116757","text":" HTML"}]},{"id":"blk-84054","spans":[{"id":"spn-116758","text":"Custom Elements"}]},{"id":"blk-84055","spans":[{"id":"spn-116759","text":"Hand-written pages, embedding inside existing apps"}]}],[{"id":"blk-84056","spans":[{"id":"spn-116760","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-116761","text":" DSL"}]},{"id":"blk-84057","spans":[{"id":"spn-116762","text":"Curly-brace declarative"}]},{"id":"blk-84058","spans":[{"id":"spn-116763","text":"Hand-authored layouts, version control reviewability"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-84059","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116764","text":"The DSL is specified in "},{"id":"spn-116765","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.dsl.md"},{"id":"spn-116766","text":". The CLI converts losslessly between all three."}]},{"id":"blk-84060","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116767","text":"9.2 Planned tree"}]},{"id":"blk-84061","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"runefort/\n  spec/\n    runefort.protocol.md       ← this document\n    runefort.core.md           ← @runefort/core web component spec\n    runefort.dsl.md            ← .rune DSL spec\n    schema.json                ← JSON schema for runefort.json\n  packages/\n    core/                      ← @runefort/core (web components, target ≤5KB)\n    cli/                       ← runefort CLI (compile/fmt/to-rune)\n    react/                     ← @runefort/react adapter (~1KB)\n    vue/                       ← @runefort/vue adapter\n    svelte/                    ← @runefort/svelte adapter\n    liveview/                  ← @runefort/liveview adapter\n  examples/\n    no-framework/              ← raw HTML, proves \"runs anywhere\"\n    supervisor-floor/          ← the [&] use case, proves supervisor-floor.v1\n    codebase-atlas/            ← non-[&], proves genericity\n    dashboard-grid/            ← non-[&], proves genericity"},{"id":"blk-84062","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116768","text":"Two non-[&] examples are required before we cut v0.1 final. Otherwise we're an [&] dashboard with a spec attached."}]},{"id":"blk-84063","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116769","text":"9.3 Build order (v0.1)"}]},{"id":"blk-84064","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84066","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116770","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"},{"id":"spn-116771","text":" — the four web components + "},{"id":"spn-116772","marks":["code"],"text":"mount(json)"},{"id":"spn-116773","text":". Smallest meaningful artifact."}]}],"id":"blk-84065","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84068","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116774","text":"Playground at runefort.com — live "},{"id":"spn-116775","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-116776","text":" editor → rendered floor. The shareable demo."}]}],"id":"blk-84067","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84070","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116777","text":"CLI compile path — "},{"id":"spn-116778","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-116779","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-116780","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-116781","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-116782","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-116783","text":" → static HTML."}]}],"id":"blk-84069","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84072","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116784","text":"Adapters — React, then LiveView, then others as demand appears."}]}],"id":"blk-84071","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-84073","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116785","text":"Adapters wait until non-zero users exist. Shipping all adapters before having users is the wrong direction of optimization."}]},{"id":"blk-84074","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116786","text":"10. Relationship to the [&] stack"}]},{"id":"blk-84075","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116787","text":"Runefort is "},{"id":"spn-116788","marks":["bold"],"text":"independent of"},{"id":"spn-116789","text":" [&]. It does not import, depend on, or require any [&] protocol. However:"}]},{"id":"blk-84076","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84078","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116790","marks":["code"],"text":"[&]"},{"id":"spn-116791","text":" capability descriptors MAY be embedded in "},{"id":"spn-116792","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-116793","text":" under "},{"id":"spn-116794","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-116795","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-84077","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84080","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116796","text":"PULSE manifest phases MAY drive room generation in tooling that bridges PULSE → Runefort."}]}],"id":"blk-84079","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84082","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116797","text":"PRISM scores MAY be a signal source for state bindings."}]}],"id":"blk-84081","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84083","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116798","text":"These are "},{"id":"spn-116799","marks":["italic"],"text":"integration patterns"},{"id":"spn-116800","text":", not protocol requirements. A Runefort layout that knows nothing about [&] is fully conformant."}]},{"id":"blk-84084","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-116801","text":"11. Open questions for v0.2"}]},{"id":"blk-84085","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84087","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116802","marks":["bold"],"text":"Nesting."},{"id":"spn-116803","text":" A room inside a room (zoomable). Worth adding to core, or push to a vocabulary?"}]}],"id":"blk-84086","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84089","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116804","marks":["bold"],"text":"Streaming layout edits."},{"id":"spn-116805","text":" Today the JSON is whole-document. Should there be a patch format?"}]}],"id":"blk-84088","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84091","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116806","marks":["bold"],"text":"Manifest discovery."},{"id":"spn-116807","text":" Does a renderer auto-discover "},{"id":"spn-116808","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-116809","text":" in a repo, or is the path always provided?"}]}],"id":"blk-84090","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84093","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116810","marks":["bold"],"text":"Multiple anchors per room."},{"id":"spn-116811","text":" Today one anchor. Real codebases have N files per logical region."}]}],"id":"blk-84092","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84094","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116812","text":"These are explicitly deferred. v0.1 ships with the four primitives and nothing else."}]},{"id":"blk-84095","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-116813","marks":["italic"],"text":"This spec is the contract. Everything in `runefort.com/docs/spec/README.md` (the spatial-cognition / dark-factory spec) is now reframed as the `supervisor-floor.v1` vocabulary plus the `runefort.dark_factory` reference application — both built on top of this protocol."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierao37bmdyxyykg7jkn3gcfkpfpv2eg4mltvhgwljjp43rqwgizriva","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}